WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.201 --> 00:00:15.571
It took almost two weeks by coach, but Jo and Beth finally arrived in California.

2
00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:22.041
Jo had reserved rooms in a small, unique hotel that also offered tours to see the wildlife, including buffalo.

3
00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:31.325
"Oh, Jo," Beth's voice shook with emotion when their tour group finally came across a herd of buffalo grazing on the fields.

4
00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:37.316
Just as Beth had thought, the massive creatures were gentle and peaceful as they carried on with their business,

5
00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:40.923
paying no attention to the humans staring at them from a distance.

6
00:00:40.924 --> 00:00:45.127
"Is this what you imagined them to be like?" Jo whispered to Beth.

7
00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:51.995
Nodding, Beth said teary eyed, "It's a dream come true. Thank you, Jo."

8
00:00:51.996 --> 00:01:00.080
Putting her arm around Beth's thin, weak shoulders, Jo took in every detail around her, for she wanted to remember this moment forever.

9
00:01:00.081 --> 00:01:06.118
After the argument with Laurie, Amy found it hard to find joy in anything, even drawing and painting.

10
00:01:06.119 --> 00:01:13.728
Laurie came by once more to tell Aunt March and her that he was leaving for Spain and wished them the best on the rest of their trip.

11
00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:20.234
"I think it's time for us to depart this place as well," Aunt March had said when Laurie left.

12
00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:25.465
"Where shall we go?" Amy asked, not really caring since she knew Laurie would not be there.

13
00:01:25.466 --> 00:01:28.243
"Florence," stated the old lady.

14
00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:36.429
But as Amy stood outside on the balcony of their villa in Florence, she felt no inspiration to paint one of the most beautiful cities in the world.

15
00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.674
All she could think about was Laurie.

16
00:01:39.675 --> 00:01:45.188
On the way back home, Jo noticed that Beth seemed to struggle more with the strenuous journey.

17
00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:51.547
She got tired easily, didn't have the energy even to look outside at the scenery, and mostly slept a lot.

18
00:01:51.548 --> 00:01:59.899
When they got home, Beth, barely able to stand, clung tightly to Jo's arm and said, "This has been the best adventure of my life, Jo.

19
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:07.110
I'll never forget it." Jo clutched her hands tightly and pressed her lips to stifle an agonizing cry.

20
00:02:07.111 --> 00:02:15.045
She would have collapsed into tears then and there if not for Mother's next words, "There's a letter for you, Jo. Actually two."

21
00:02:15.046 --> 00:02:20.273
As Mother handed them over to her, Jo recognized the strong handwriting of the Professor.

22
00:02:20.274 --> 00:02:25.450
After putting Beth to bed, Jo took the letters upstairs to her sanctuary.

23
00:02:25.451 --> 00:02:33.987
As she read them, her spirits lifted. She even laughed as she imagined the Professor speaking aloud in his German accent and calling her "Cho."

24
00:02:33.988 --> 00:02:39.334
Holding the letters close to her chest, Jo found the strength to bear the pain that was ahead.

25
00:02:39.335 --> 00:02:42.441
A few months passed with no hope of Beth getting better.

26
00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:49.887
Without strength to sit, Beth was confined to her bed, which was moved downstairs so she could look out into the street and garden.

27
00:02:49.888 --> 00:02:54.086
"Jo, can you read me a story?" Beth would ask.

28
00:02:54.087 --> 00:03:00.406
When Jo brought over a book, Beth would move her head from side to side and say, "Leave me alone."

29
00:03:00.407 --> 00:03:05.471
Jo felt helpless, because she wanted to ease her sister's pain but didn't know how.

30
00:03:05.472 --> 00:03:13.262
Mother seemed to deal better with the situation, bringing things for Beth just when she needed them and leaving her in peace when she wanted to rest.

31
00:03:13.263 --> 00:03:19.643
Meg, who now knew that she was indeed carrying twins, also spent every day by Beth's side.

32
00:03:19.644 --> 00:03:25.151
"Feel the babies kicking, Beth," Meg would say, placing Beth's limp hand over her growing stomach.

33
00:03:25.152 --> 00:03:29.098
"I felt it, Meg," Beth would say, her eyes filling with tears.

34
00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:33.240
"You're going to be an auntie soon, darling," Meg would remind her.

35
00:03:33.241 --> 00:03:39.616
But Beth would only smile weakly and say, "I hope they're girls, and they're as beautiful as you."

36
00:03:39.617 --> 00:03:46.978
One afternoon, Jo, not wanting to disturb Beth, crept over to refill the water pitcher on the table next to Beth's bed.

37
00:03:46.979 --> 00:03:49.529
"Jo?" Beth called softly.

38
00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:53.460
"Yes, darling? Did I wake you?" Jo asked.

39
00:03:53.461 --> 00:03:58.958
Beth shook her head slightly as if to say no, then said, "Will you lie here with me?"

40
00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:03.376
Jo carefully got into the bed next to her sister and wrapped her arm around her.

41
00:04:03.377 --> 00:04:07.447
"I'm here, Beth. Do you want me to tell you a story?"

42
00:04:07.448 --> 00:04:14.791
Beth blinked her eyes once and sighed. "Jo? I'm ready to go now."

43
00:04:14.792 --> 00:04:23.062
Jo, not wanting to part with her sister yet, gently squeezed Beth's shoulders and said, "Hold on just a little longer, Beth.

44
00:04:23.063 --> 00:04:26.343
Meg's babies are coming and Amy will be home soon.

45
00:04:26.344 --> 00:04:28.994
Be strong for just a little longer . . ."

46
00:04:28.995 --> 00:04:36.533
But Beth turned her head, looked at her sister tenderly, then closed her eyes, and died in Jo's arms.

47
00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:41.752
When Beth's funeral was held a few days later, almost everyone from the town was there.

48
00:04:41.753 --> 00:04:48.393
Although the family had sent a telegram to Amy about her sister's death, they urged her to stay with Aunt March for the rest of the trip,

49
00:04:48.394 --> 00:04:51.457
because that was what Beth had wished.

50
00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:56.519
At home the March family had to rebuild their lives after the loss of beloved Beth.

51
00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:02.687
Mother, who had been so strong throughout Beth's illness, seemed to age decades in a matter of days afterward.

52
00:05:02.688 --> 00:05:06.199
Still, she found comfort in the loving arms of her husband.

53
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:11.600
Both Mother and Father tried to give each other strength to cope with the loss of one of their children.

54
00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:17.868
However, Jo was inconsolable. No amount of kind words or deeds could soothe the pain in her heart.

55
00:05:17.869 --> 00:05:24.591
Every day she escaped into the woods, taking long walks by herself with her memories of her sweet sister.

56
00:05:24.592 --> 00:05:31.754
A few weeks after Beth's death, Jo was just clearing up the dishes from dinner when John came running into the house.

57
00:05:31.755 --> 00:05:36.642
"Please, come quickly," he said breathlessly. "Meg is having the babies!"

58
00:05:36.643 --> 00:05:42.351
Mother, Father, Jo, and Hannah raced out, leaving the dishes and other worries behind.

59
00:05:42.352 --> 00:05:47.039
When they got to the house, Dr. Bangs and a midwife were already there with Meg.

60
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:52.576
Mother went into the room with them while Jo, John, and Father paced the living room anxiously.

61
00:05:52.577 --> 00:05:56.124
A few hours later, they heard a baby crying.

62
00:05:56.125 --> 00:06:02.919
"Oh John!" Jo cried, holding onto her brother-in-law's hand. "Congratulations!"

63
00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:10.030
Then shortly after, another cry erupted, and they could hear laughter and cries from behind the door.

64
00:06:10.031 --> 00:06:13.030
"John?" Dr. Bangs called, opening the door.

65
00:06:13.031 --> 00:06:17.480
"Come in and see your babies. Come, Mr. March. You too, Jo and Hannah."

66
00:06:17.481 --> 00:06:22.708
Everyone crowded into the room where Meg sat up holding one baby in the crook of each arm.

67
00:06:22.709 --> 00:06:31.265
"This is your new son," she said, looking at the bundle on her right, then pointed her chin toward the left, adding, "and your new daughter."

68
00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:37.110
Everyone started hugging and crying as they welcomed the newest members of the family into the world.

69
00:06:37.111 --> 00:06:43.052
Jo looked lovingly at her niece and nephew and realized for a sad moment that they would never see their Aunt Beth.

70
00:06:43.053 --> 00:06:50.095
However, Jo promised to do what she could to help them get acquainted with the wonderful aunt who had died before their birth.

71
00:06:50.096 --> 00:06:54.138
"What are you going to name them, Meg? John?" asked Father.

72
00:06:54.139 --> 00:06:57.631
"Daisy and Demi," the happy parents said together.

73
00:06:57.632 --> 00:07:05.983
"Welcome to your family," the new grandfather said proudly.
